<Article
  title="A label, later"
  description="Return to Aura. One beautiful room at a time."
  kicker="Later"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>The farm wall can already be asked for. Thirst Contact, the water unit, comes later and still needs further research. A wider network around either of them does not exist yet. This note is that plan, written so it cannot be mistaken for a signup.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">The label</RevealHeading>
  <p>An advertiser’s name may one day sit on a harvest or a jug. That is a placement, and it is not live. If that network is ever built, Aura would place the rooms and the label.</p>
  <p>The same room can skip that idea. An owner who buys a farm wall can keep the harvest. A bottling line, once Thirst Contact is past research, could be used the same way. The network is a choice for later. The farm unit is the choice available to ask about now.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What the network means here</RevealHeading>
  <p>It would mean a repeated way to place rooms, fill jugs, harvest a wall, and carry an advertiser’s label under one set of rules. It does not mean a territory for sale, a fee schedule, or a brand you can license this month. There is no advertiser marketplace on this site.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">Why say it now</RevealHeading>
  <p>The rooms, the <a href="/farms">farm walls</a>, and the <a href="/water">water unit</a> are easier to understand if the longer aim is visible. People who only want a room should still be able to find the room, and stop there. People who want to grow can ask for a farm unit. People who want water from the air can read the Thirst Contact page and wait for the research.</p>
  <p>Until an advertiser has actually placed a label, the honest sentence is this: the network is not live.</p>
</Article>
